<div class="article-body">
    <div class="callout">
      <h2 id="glance" style="margin-top:0">At a glance</h2>
      <ol class="stop-steps">
        <li><strong>Evidence:</strong> no randomized trial has tested dead hangs for impingement or rotator cuff problems (Europe PMC search, October 2026).</li>
        <li><strong>Source of the idea:</strong> surgeon John M. Kirsch proposed overhead hanging in a self-published book. It is a hypothesis.</li>
        <li><strong>Which hang first:</strong> many people start with a passive hang and keep their feet on the ground to share the load.</li>
        <li><strong>Stop</strong> for sharp, catching or electrical pain. Ask a clinician first with an injury, surgery or an unstable shoulder.</li>
